# Deprecations

## Purpose

Prevent accidental changes to known-legacy code awaiting a planned migration.

## When Applied

Touching legacy code under `lib/view/**`, the deprecation list, or when asked to "clean up"/refactor.

## Requirements

- Treat `lib/view/`, the unused `provider` dependency, `navigation_bloc.dart`, and other listed items as **frozen** — leave them alone unless explicitly asked.
- Legacy `Supabase.instance` usage in admin scan/tracking/QR is tolerated but must **not** be extended into new code.
- Record any new deprecation intent in [`docs/deprecation-list.md`](../../../docs/deprecation-list.md); don't delete in the same pass.
- Migrations off legacy are separate, explicitly-scoped tasks.

## Examples

- Building a new screen → put it in `lib/features/`, not `lib/view/`.

## Anti-patterns

- Deleting or "modernizing" a legacy screen while shipping an unrelated feature.
- Copying a legacy pattern into a new module.

## Common Mistakes

- Removing the unused `provider` dependency as a "cleanup".
- Assuming a legacy file is dead and deleting it without confirmation.
